  "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B001",
        "laureates": [
          "Kazutoshi Mori",
          "Peter Walter"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of the unfolded protein response and signaling from the endoplasmic reticulum"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B024",
    "B007"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B001 remains my preferred configuration because it identifies a fundamental and coherent physiological system by which cells sense and adapt to endoplasmic-reticulum stress. The discovery has exceptional mechanistic depth, broad explanatory reach across cell biology and disease, and long independent maturation. Mori and Walter remain a focused, complementary attribution for the central signaling discoveries.",
    "case_against": "The response encompasses multiple signaling arms and a broader community of contributors, so the historical boundary of the discovery requires careful review. Its medical consequences are also less directly demonstrable at the patient level than those of the leading therapeutic candidates.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson places GLP-1 physiology first, stressing its major therapeutic transformation in diabetes and obesity while noting difficult attribution between foundational biology and pharmaceutical development.",
        "response": "I agree that B024 has extraordinary clinical importance and is a serious alternative. However, the attribution boundary is materially more crowded, whereas B001 offers an unusually compact connection between a defined discovery, its principal discoverers, and a mature mechanistic framework."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius places TNF blockade first because Feldmann and Maini unite pathogenic insight with decisive, durable clinical translation.",
        "response": "B007 is exceptionally strong in direct medical benefit and has a persuasive two-person attribution. I give B001 a narrow preference because the unfolded protein response constituted a foundational biological framework with broad and sustained consequences, while recognizing that B007 may better satisfy a preference for direct therapeutic transformation."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg ranks antisense correction of SMN2 splicing first as a precise molecular intervention that transformed spinal muscular atrophy.",
        "response": "The clinical achievement of B008 is compelling and the mechanism-to-treatment trajectory is unusually clear. I would nevertheless place it behind B001 at present because attribution extends beyond the proposed pair into disease biology and therapeutic development, and its broader platform implications remain less historically settled."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the central UPR discoveries can be delimited sufficiently from parallel and subsequent work on its multiple signaling branches.",
      "How to weigh a fundamental cellular discovery against more immediately transformative therapeutic advances."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
